# Default owners for everything in this repository.
# Organization-wide policy, templates and shared workflows change rarely and
# affect every repo, so all changes here need maintainer review.
#
# A username rather than a team, because there is one maintainer and no team
# exists. GitHub silently ignores an owner it cannot resolve, so naming a team
# that does not exist means no review is requested at all. Switch these to a
# team on the day that team exists and has more than one person in it.

*                               @martin-k-m

